WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.940
Good morning John! I can already hear the music building up beneath me so I should probably just

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.840
stop talking. This song is about quarks, I wrote it, it's called "Strange Charm".

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.880
[singing] A Quark is a fundamental constituent of matter

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.260
Observed in 1968 through deep elastic scatter

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.100
We found that protons aren't as simple as we thought

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.820
We thought they were solid particles but they are not

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.440
Protons in fact are made up of 3 separate pieces

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.080
It just gets more confusing as our knowledge increases

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.080
But that is what a quark is, it's a piece of a proton

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.660
And they also make up other things including the neutron

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:37.400
Oh up down strange charm top bottom, if you don't know what a quark is, it don't matter you still got 'em

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.900
And with leptons and bosons unless something's amiss

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.540
They make up everything that we can see and that we know exists.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.220
Things made up of quarks including protons and neutrons

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:48.500
are composite particles that physicists call hadrons

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.540
many types of hadrons are theoretically described

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:53.500
but most exist for only very brief amounts of time

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.200
quarks have electric charge, color charge mass and spin

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.520
and having color charge means they exist solely

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.760
inside of other kinds of particles and cannot exist alone

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.540
which is why quarks have never been studied on their own

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.960
up down strange charm top bottom. If you don't know what a quark is it don't matter, you still got 'em

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.380
and with leptons and bosons unless something's amiss

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:15.360
they make up everything that we can see and that we know exists

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.280
quarks can join together in two different ways

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:20.620
baryons and mesons but most instantly decay

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:23.420
if a particle has three quarks then it's a baryon

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.320
and if there's one quark and an anti-quark then it is a meson

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:29.020
these tiny bits of matter are part of almost everything

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.680
and there is no unified theory to make it less confusing

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.400
but the fact that we've identified that they exist at all

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.800
is so goddamn remarkable that I just sit in awe

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:42.600
oh, up down strange charm top bottom if you don't know what a quark is it don't matter you still got 'em

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.960
and with leptons and bosons unless sonething's amiss

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:48.100
